    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "The absolute value equation means there may be two cases:\n$n + 6 = 2 - n$ or $n + 6 = - (2 - n)$.\n\nSo,\n$n + 6 = 2 - n$ gives $n - n = 2 - 6$; and this simplifies to $0 = -4$, which is not true.\n\n$n + 6 = - (2 - n)$ gives $n + 6 = -2 + n$.  Simplifying, $6 = -2$, which is since there is no number that makes this true.\n\nHence, there is no solution for this equation.\n\n\\boxed{n \\text{ is not a real number}}",
