    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the equation |n + 6| = 2 - n, we need to consider the definition of absolute value.\nIf n + 6 is non-negative, then |n + 6| = n + 6. In this case, the equation becomes:\nn + 6 = 2 - n\n2n = -4\nn = -2\n\nIf n + 6 is negative, then |n + 6| = -(n + 6). In this case, the equation becomes:\n-(n + 6) = 2 - n\nn + 6 = 2 - n\n2n = -4\nn = -2\n\nSo, we found that n = -2 satisfies the given equation.\nAnswer: \\boxed{n = -2}",
